{"requirements":[{"id":"system_account","requirement":"A system account named inventorysvc exists on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The account was absent initially, then created with useradd --system. Direct checks showed UID 992 below UID_MIN 1000, and the account remained present after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-35d1068077274210","cmd-f6518c9f08284fac","cmd-013f84f7071a455e","cmd-ab5bef9eb0f34411"]},{"id":"home_directory","requirement":"inventorysvc has /var/lib/inventory as its home directory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Successful assertions verified the passwd home field, directory existence, and inventorysvc ownership before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-013f84f7071a455e","cmd-ab5bef9eb0f34411"]},{"id":"no_interactive_login","requirement":"inventorysvc has no interactive login access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Successful assertions verified /sbin/nologin as the shell, and direct su attempts were rejected with 'This account is currently not available' both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-013f84f7071a455e","cmd-ab5bef9eb0f34411"]}],"confidence":1.0,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account creation was the required retained change (cmd-f6518c9f08284fac). The scheduled reboot was necessary for the mandatory restart protocol and completed successfully (cmd-ced02a7c0984471f). Other commands were read-only checks or bounded login/recovery probes. Afterward, package health remained clean, no failed services appeared, and listeners were unchanged apart from expected post-reboot process IDs.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f6518c9f08284fac","cmd-ced02a7c0984471f","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct pre- and post-restart verification. The sole managed node also completed the restart protocol: a healthy task state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, connection loss was observed, the boot identity changed, the system returned to running state, and the account and home configuration recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":[]}
